    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from the v1 API to v2.\n\n**Changes**\n- Switched endpoint from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Replaced the single-response query with the paged `settlements(first: 100, after: ...)` connection query.\n- Traverses by `pageInfo.hasNextPage`, so short or empty pages no longer end the run prematurely.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last version received (amended settlements).\n- Restarts traversal without `after` if the server rejects an expired/malformed cursor.\n\n**Verified against the live v2 server at `http://the VM's public address:18081`**\n- 27 pages fetched successfully.\n- 1,873 unique settlements written.\n- Output contained no duplicate IDs, no missing IDs, and no value mismatches.\n- The traversal included 4 empty pages, 9 short pages, and 19 re-delivered amended settlements \u2014 all handled correctly.\n- Cursor-error restart behavior was also exercised with a simulated expired cursor.",
